<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Llancarfan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Llancarfan is a village in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vale-of-glamorgan">Vale of Glamorgan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, site of a monastery founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-cadoc">Saint Cadoc</a> in the 6th century. It was one of the leading churches of early medieval south Wales and a centre of learning, where Caradog of Llancarfan wrote saints' lives in the 12th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/llancarfan.jpg" alt="Llancarfan" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The National Churches Trust · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Llancarfan,_St_Cadoc_(35873785235).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
